WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.610
- All right y'all, I'm still here

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.060
keeping up with my social
distancing with my family

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.590
here in Montana.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.840
This hour thou we're gonna
be celebrating my new single,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:08.673
I dare you.

00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:11.200
That I actually got to record
in six different languages,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.240
which was really a dream come true for me.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.430
This song is about love in all it's forms,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.020
in the face of adversity,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.650
you know choosing to love instead of fear.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.460
I'm proud that the singers
from all over the world

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.460
sang with me on this track.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.960
I love all the different languages.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.100
I actually listen to those
more than the english version.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.600
But we're singing in
their native languages

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.700
and we're so excited that we actually

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.360
have them on Zoom today.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.240
We have Blas from España.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.570
We have Faouzia from Morocco.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.270
We have Carolin from Germany,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.110
and we also have Maya from Israel.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.340
How Y'all doing?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.700
- Hey Kelly!

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.270
- Well okay guys, we're
all here officially.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.560
Blas like what are you
doing, like right now?

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.610
Like how are you handling the quarantine?

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.540
- Yeah, I'm good.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.510
A few days before the stay-home
order I was visiting my mom

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.900
and I could not go back home to Madrid.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.180
And here I am, I'm good.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.900
I'm happy because I found myself again,

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.900
I can, I can see the, all the
pictures and it's beautiful.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.810
- Awesome.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.060
- Oh what about you Carolin?

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.380
What are you doing, in Germany?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.250
How are you hanging?

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.600
- Yeah, I'm doing good,
I'm staying home of course.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.450
And yeah, I'm trying to make
the best of the situation

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.620
we are all in.
- Yeah.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.340
- Yeah and I try to focus on some stuff

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.510
that is left undone at home

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:39.300
like cleaning out my closet
(giggling) everything.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.390
- Oh my God I have organized
everything. (laughing)

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.500
- Yeah, me too (laughing).

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.820
Yeah but, but most
importantly I have enough time

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.640
to write some songs for
my band, Glasperlenspiel.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.690
I think it's,
- Yeah,

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.940
kind of good to stay
at home now, and yeah.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.321
- All right, well what about you Faouzia,

00:01:57.321 --> 00:01:59.680
what are you doing right now?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.800
You're in Canada right?

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.210
- Yes, thankfully I've
been doing really well

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:06.940
and I've been keeping busy,
working around these conditions

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.050
and making a lot of music at home

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.480
and I even got to make
a music video from home.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.850
Which was a new experience.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:14.683
- Oh my God.

00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:16.330
- And I've just been praying,

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.700
you know for all the lives lost

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.920
and I just hope--
- Yeah.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.190
everybody's taking this seriously.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:22.880
- All right well Maya, what's up with you?

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.230
How are you hanging?

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:27.154
- Well actually I'm now in a show,

00:02:27.154 --> 00:02:31.330
(audio lost) like yours in Israel.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.803
- Oh.
- We are shooting, right now.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.240
- Wow.
- And I'm so excited,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.487
that is not here you
know because it's you.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.140
- Okay, I couldn't hear the
last bit but I love you.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.316
But it's cutting out. (everyone laughing)

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:48.620
- So okay, so here's my question I choose.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.200
You know the song is about
daring to love instead of fear.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.440
So what's the most selfless thing

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.250
that someone has done for you

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.070
that really kind of stands out for you?

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:57.903
Blas you can go.

00:02:57.903 --> 00:03:01.400
- A few days ago I remembered
that I had a problem

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.200
with on our computer here at home,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.950
and I asked of course somebody
to help me on Instagram

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.980
and a boy sent me a direct message.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.650
We were repairing that thing
together the whole day.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.483
- What, a stranger?

00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:18.510
- Yes, it was great.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.180
Now I have a new friend and
a new computer. (laughing)

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.450
- That's so great,

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.642
what a nice thing.
- Yeah.

00:03:24.642 --> 00:03:25.634
- Amazing.
- You just put it

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:26.980
on the internet and then
somebody helped you,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.520
that's so cool.
- Yes.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.800
- Well Carolin, what about you?

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:34.800
- Yeah, selfless is what
my mother did to me.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:38.950
We went through some tough
times after my father left us

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.950
and yeah, she worked, she
was always working so hard

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.300
to make my dreams and wishes come true

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.070
and I'm so thankful for that

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.910
because she's the reason
why I had the chance

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.490
to become a musician and yeah,

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.420
without her I wouldn't be where I am now,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.160
so I'm, yeah, I'm very thankful for that.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.850
- That's so cool, we
have a very similar story

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.350
after you just said that.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.970
So what about you Faouzia?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:04.970
- Kind of the same thing

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.820
but both my parents have been like very,

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.480
obviously very selfless and I think that,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.310
I think that the love of,
you know, your parents

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.880
or your parents or who ever it may be

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.760
and you know that they don't
expect anything in return.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.770
It's like, kind of scary but
it's also a very pure feeling

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:28.770
and I honestly owe everything
to them and to my family.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:30.920
- Your parents sound amazing,

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.490
I remember you talking
about them in the studio.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.650
You're a very lucky kid, that's so cool.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.483
- You're not a kid,
- Thank you.

00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:37.316
You're just a kid to me

00:04:37.316 --> 00:04:38.866
'cause I'm like so much older than you.

00:04:38.866 --> 00:04:40.360
(laughing)

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.825
- I have a daughter
your age (mumbling) so.

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:44.658
(laughing)

00:04:44.658 --> 00:04:46.850
But, Maya what about, what about you?

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.693
- Since I've been a mother it's,

00:04:48.693 --> 00:04:53.250
it's amazing, it's like to
see a little person loves you,

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.487
just free love with no, even
in this horrible situation,

00:04:57.487 --> 00:05:00.220
during Corona that all the kids are home

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.400
and they are suffering from, you know,

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.100
doing nothing or study at home,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.607
he's just selfless, he's like:

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:12.490
"Okay Mommy, just here you
are, just for you to be happy."

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.950
And for me it's the most incredible thing

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.749
just to,
- Yeah.

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:21.925
- to appreciate free
love, you know, with no...

00:05:21.925 --> 00:05:24.693
- No strings attached.
- I hope all the people

00:05:24.693 --> 00:05:26.640
will be like this after this Corona.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.400
- Yeah, well thank you guys so much.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.337
The song is very meaningful for me

00:05:30.337 --> 00:05:32.810
and the project is very meaningful for me.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.800
And it's even more meaningful

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.353
that y'all elevated it so
much with your languages.

